 992	     *
 993	     * A player with several naked colonies clicks through all of them before logging off, and the
 994	     * invariant reads the account, so one login has to reach them all: a pass that returned a single
 995	     * sibling per login needed as many logins as the account has planets, which is longer than its
 996	     * own day of sessions, and the cohort read still found planets at zero beside a sibling holding
 997	     * a wall (QUAL-003: 3 planets at zero defence while one held 1,312 units). Each order names its
 998	     * own planet, so the schedule places them on the planets that stand bare, whatever the login chose.
 999	     *
1000	     * The order a bare sibling takes is the wall itself when its own yard can build it, and the
1001	     * building planner's wall prerequisites stand the yard when it cannot: a login that finds a
1002	     * sibling naked beside a wall spends itself on that sibling before the account's habits. Each
1003	     * order names the planet it belongs to, so the executor places it on that planet and not on
1004	     * whichever planet the login happened to open.
1005	     *
1006	     * Only an account that already holds a wall somewhere is served: while no wall stands anywhere
1007	     * the account is in its opening, where cargo, the colony ship and the probe come first, and the
1008	     * standing pass below still reaches the floor once a wall exists. A planet already paid for in
1009	     * the yard is no longer bare and is left for the next login.
1010	     *
1011	     * A sibling whose own yard cannot take the wall yet is left to the building planner: the order
1012	     * this pass can place is a defence unit, and a login that can neither place the unit nor stand
1013	     * the yard it waits on keeps the sibling naked, so the yard is the planner's own pass and not
1014	     * a second facility decision here. A sibling that can take the unit but holds nothing is served
1015	     * here whatever its exposure, so the wall reaches every planet the account owns.
1016	     *
1017	     * @return list<QueueableUnit>
